      "linkedin_copy": "Most engineers have experimented with AI by asking for code snippets and pasting them into their workflow. While this approach is useful, it barely scratches the surface of leading techniques for agentic code development. AI-assisted instrumentation is no longer speculative or distant — it’s emerging rapidly and already usable today.\nHosted by Tech Briefs, this 45-minute technical on-demand webinar explores how engineers can move beyond copy-paste prompting toward context-driven, plan-first AI workflows that actively control instruments, analyze data, and generate results in real time.\n You'll learn how AI can:\nWrite automation code\nConfigure oscilloscopes and signal source\nExecute measurements and perform math and plotting\nAutomatically export structured data\n Watch now to explore emerging AI‑assisted instrumentation.   https://app.webinar.net/Gp5d8bMWAxR\n\n",
